<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5594" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bō^trys</span></b> , yos,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βότρυς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Latinized <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bō^trus</span></b> , i,
			f. (cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 17, 5,
			14</span></i>), <i>the grape</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Mic. 7, 1</span></i> (as transl. of the
			Heb. ).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In the Greek form botrys, <i>a plant</i>,
				<i>also called</i> artemisia, <i>mugwort</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 7, 36, § 74</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">27, 4, 11, §
				28</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
